# Faneqo backend safety

Inspect existing implementation before modifying it. Smallest safe change.

## Database

- No destructive production DB work casually
- No auto-merging fans — classify SAFE / CONFLICTING / UNKNOWN
- Audit / dry-run before risky migrations
- Preserve idempotency
- Fail closed

## Boot and deploy

- Boot-critical new modules/imports need a basic require/boot test (`scripts/test-labs-boot-requires.js` is the pattern)
- Before backend deploy: relevant tests + boot/import test
- After backend deploy: `GET /api/health` → 200 **and** inspect Railway startup logs
- GitHub/deploy success alone does not prove Strapi is healthy

## Performance and scope

- Avoid N+1; prefer grouped/bulk helpers
- No external provider APIs on normal interactive dashboard paths
- No Redis, Kafka, materialized views, or microservices without measured need
- No broad refactors outside the current phase
- Do not commit, push, deploy, reset, restore, or stash unless explicitly instructed
